We keep the idle bias large negative to avoid idle actions and focus on left/right decisions. By reducing the left‑action velocity weight from -4 to -3.5 we make left pushes slightly less aggressive when velocity is negative, helping to prevent premature left‑wall bounces. Increasing the right‑action position weight to 1.0 adds a modest position bias that encourages choosing the right action earlier as the car moves rightward, while the strong velocity weight (5.8) retains the needed positive‑velocity push. This combination should balance the swing‑up energy transfer better and aim for an episode length near the expected optimum (~‑120).
