The left‐action row only depends on velocity (−5.3·v), encouraging left thrust when the car is moving left. The “no‑thrust” action stays a constant −5.3, so it is never chosen unless both left and right scores are low. The right‑action row now places a stronger emphasis on position (7.2·x) together with velocity (6.5·v), biasing the policy to accelerate right earlier as the car reaches the right side of the valley. By increasing the right‑action position weight we aim to build forward momentum more aggressively, reducing the number of steps to reach the flag.
